I'm afraid and quite comfortable.
I'm afraid I'll get in trouble.
I'm afraid I'll worry about my fears
  -- and make them double.
I'm afraid I'll singalong and get the words wrong
  -- like that one song that I always indeed sing wrong.
I'm afraid of the color of bronze on my bedroom doorknobs
  and the ferrings of my ceiling fan
  -- which just keeps spinning, man.

